<<<
analogy (Log., Gram.); ‘ accordance with proportion’. Inference
===
*analogy* (Log., Gram.); ‘accordance with proportion’. Inference
>>>

<<<
resembles that of a person, must b lapse of time grow feeble & die is analogical.
===
resembles that of a person, must by lapse of time grow feeble & die is analogical.
>>>

<<<
Since opera resembles drama both in being the name of a play & in ending in -a, analogy provides opera with the (incorrect) adj. operatic to match the rightly formed dramatic.
===
Since *opera* resembles *drama* both in being the name of a play & in ending in *-a*, analogy provides *opera* with the (incorrect) adj. *operatic* to match the rightly formed *dramatic*.
>>>

